{
  "run_id": "PMC12941970__problem_constrained__web64k_r2_b_o3mini__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi matrix has a homogeneous microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Plain CoCrFeNi has limited ability to maintain low friction and wear at high temperatures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is addition of 5–10 at.% Cu to CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cu acts as a reactive-element alloying addition in CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cu addition promotes formation of a continuous oxide glaze during sliding.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The sliding-induced oxide glaze is lubricious.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide glaze adapts across the range from room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "During sliding, Cu preferentially oxidizes.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preferential Cu oxidation produces a dense and adherent oxide layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At lower temperatures, the oxide layer smoothens contact asperities.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At lower temperatures, the oxide layer reduces adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, the oxide layer becomes more reactive and more resistant to plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A dense glaze layer at 800 °C can reduce adhesive and oxidative wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to plain CoCrFeNi, the Cu-alloyed variant will have a lower and more stable coefficient of friction throughout the full temperature range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10730726::web::019::effect_of_input_parameters_on_cof"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to plain CoCrFeNi, the Cu-alloyed variant will have a lower wear rate throughout the full temperature range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Abrasive and oxidative wear mechanisms cause the baseline CoCrFeNi alloy's high-temperature tribological limitations.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed operating boundary is dry sliding in ambient air from approximately 25 °C to 800 °C under loads of 5–30 N.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    }
  ],
